  "worked_solution": "If $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables with the joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the corresponding joint CDF is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(X\\le x,Y\\le y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v.\n$$\n\nLet's draw the region $D$ in the $uv$-plane where the function $f(u,v)$ is nonzero. Let's also consider a point $(x,y)$ where $0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,$ and a region $Δ$ that lies below and to the left of this point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14274884/assets/e4aef49bebaf250fa93e0ad1daccbad324bf714c7e5627f5245ea8387bc8da87.png)\n\nFor the purposes of computation, we're only interested in the region inside $Δ$ where $f(x,y)$ is nonzero. This is given by\n\n$$\nD\\cap Δ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le x,\\,0\\le v\\le y\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v & ={\\int }_{0}^{y}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{12}u{v}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{1}{12}{v}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}u\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{1}{12}{v}^{2}{[\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}]}_{u=0}^{u=x}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{1}{24}{x}^{2}{v}^{2}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}{x}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}{v}^{2}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}{x}^{2}{[\\frac{{v}^{3}}{3}]}_{v=0}^{v=y} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{72}{x}^{2}{y}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
